 "title": "How to Answer Salary Expectations",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This post explains how to professionally answer the common interview question regarding salary expectations. The creator demonstrates how to pitch a range based on research and value while remaining open to discussing the overall compensation package and benefits.",
 "key_points": [
  "Base your answer on research for the role and the value you bring.",
  "State a specific range, such as 22 to 25 LPA.",
  "Emphasize that you are looking for the right fit and overall package, not just a fixed salary.",
  "If the employer says the amount is above budget, acknowledge their perspective.",
  "Explain that you want a stable opportunity and want to avoid joining only to look for a new job in a couple of months.",
  "Be open to a holistic discussion covering joining bonus, relocation allowances, leaves, and work-from-home policies."
 ],
 "content": "Instagram reel/post by Sanjana Singh | Career • Money • Tech.\nText / caption:\nWhat are your salary expectations?\nComment your views and how one should address this question.\n#career #salary #jobs #corporatelife #corporate\n\nTranscript:\nSo what are your salary expectations?\nBased on my research for the role and also the value that I bring to the table, I'm looking at somewhere around 22 to 25 LPA. Uh having said that I'm more keen on getting the right fit as well as the right overall package. So not just focused on say the fixed salary pertaining to it but also the benefits part of it.\nWell, that's above our budget. Can you come down?\nI completely understand your point of view and as much as I would want to join your organisation I also want to be mindful that I don't join and you know stay disappointed and start looking out in a couple of months. I really do not want to do this because at this point of time I'm looking at a more stable opportunity.\nAh having said that I am open to having a discussion from a holistic point of view not just say salary persective but what benefits it come with. For example we can discuss about joining bonus, relocation allowances, leaves, work from home policies. So if you could look at all these aspects I think it would be nice.\n\nImportant text shown on screen:\n- So what are your salary expectations?\n- Based on my research for the role and also the value that I bring to the table, I'm looking at somewhere around 22 to 25 LPA\n- Uh having said that I'm more keen on getting the right fit as well as the right overall package\n- So not just focused on say the fixed salary pertaining to it but also the benefits part of it\n- Well, that's above our budget. Can you come down?\n- I completely understand your point of view and as much as I would want to join your organisation I also want to be mindful that I don't join and you know stay disappointed and start looking out in a couple of months\n- I really do not want to do this because at this point of time I'm looking at a more stable opportunity\n- Ah having said that I am open to having a discussion from a holistic point of view not just say salary per But what benefits it come with\n- For example we can discuss about joining bonus, relocation allowances,\n- leaves, work from home policies\n- So if you could look at all these aspects I think it would be nice",
